{
  "name": "Probe — why the four bare report roots refuse, and what the error paths look like",
  "grant": 1000,
  "notes": [
    "Every call here is expected to fail. A 400 and a 401 are free on the live API, so the",
    "whole plan costs nothing unless a probe unexpectedly succeeds — which is the result we",
    "are looking for.",
    "capture.py retries unbilled failures rather than recording them as settled, so re-running",
    "this plan re-probes rather than replaying."
  ],
  "calls": [
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/company/report/", "params": {"symbol": "BBCA"}, "est_cost": 1, "note": "symbol as a query parameter — the spec calls it a path parameter"},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/company/report/", "params": {"symbols": "BBCA"}, "est_cost": 1, "note": "plural"},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/company/report/", "params": {"ticker": "BBCA"}, "est_cost": 1, "note": "alternate name"},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/company/report/", "params": {"stock": "BBCA"}, "est_cost": 1, "note": "alternate name"},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/company/report/", "params": {"q": "BBCA"}, "est_cost": 1, "note": "screener-style"},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/company/report/", "params": {}, "est_cost": 1, "note": "bare, no parameters at all"},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/subsector/report/", "params": {"sub_sector": "banks"}, "est_cost": 1},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/subsector/report/", "params": {"sector": "banks"}, "est_cost": 1},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/subsector/report/", "params": {"subsector": "banks"}, "est_cost": 1},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/sgx/company/report/", "params": {"symbol": "D05.SI"}, "est_cost": 1},
    {"tier": 9, "path": "/v2/klse/company/report/", "params": {"symbol": "2089"}, "est_cost": 1}
  ]
